# Cursor Rules — korays-framework
# These rules are loaded automatically by Cursor IDE.

## Project
Python library implementing a 9-step Koray-style topical authority SEO pipeline.
Entry-point: pipeline.py (CLI). Core library: korays/ package.

## Language & Version
- Python >= 3.9
- Always add `from __future__ import annotations` as the first import

## Code Style
- Type hints on every function signature and dataclass field
- Use `@dataclass` for all data transfer objects (Seed, Brief, ScoredBrief, LinkedBrief)
- Use `logging.getLogger(__name__)` — never `print()` in library code
- Follow the existing module docstring format: `"""Step N — Title.\n\nDescription.\n"""`

## Architecture Rules
- No circular imports: each korays module may only import from earlier pipeline steps
- pipeline.py is the sole orchestrator — do not add orchestration logic to library modules
- Every new public class must be exported from korays/__init__.py

## Pipeline Data Flow
list[str] URLs → list[Seed] → pd.DataFrame → (+ cluster col) → list[Brief]
  → list[ScoredBrief] → list[LinkedBrief] → list[str] (output file paths)

## Testing
- Test file: tests/test_pipeline.py
- Run: `python -m pytest tests/ -v`
- Use synthetic in-memory data only; no real HTTP calls in tests
- Mock `requests.get` with `unittest.mock.patch` for SeedCollector tests

## Key Files to Understand First
1. pipeline.py          — shows the complete data flow
2. korays/__init__.py   — public API surface
3. tests/test_pipeline.py — shows expected behaviour of each class
4. agent.md             — full technical reference
